# Copy to .env.local for local overrides. Vite reads .env / .env.local and only
# exposes variables prefixed with VITE_.
#
#   NOTE: Vite does NOT read this file. Editing .env.example changes nothing —
#   copy it to .env.local first.
#
# You normally do not need to set anything here.
#
# By default the app calls the API at the SAME ORIGIN it was served from
# (`/api/v1`), and the Vite dev server proxies `/api` to http://127.0.0.1:8000
# (see vite.config.ts). That is what makes VS Code port forwarding / ngrok work:
# forward port 5173 only, and the API is reached through it. No CORS involved.
#
# Set this ONLY if the API lives on a different host from the page — for example
# a deployed backend:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/api/v1
